{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:e577203c5f4dbcc8","name":"Charlatan","source":{"id":"source:reference-e577203c5f4dbcc8","title":"Charlatan","revision":25231,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:13:36Z","sha256":"d9ad86aa11d75b5a3411b5f463aeb2d057eb6250dcdd8781821f1d9069ab926e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25231","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Charlatan&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-e577203c5f4dbcc8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Found in seedy spaceports throughout the galaxy, Charlatans are swindlers and con artists, thieves of the highest order. They specialize in double-cross, using graft, deception, and misdirection to part their victims from their hard-earned credits. Charlatans have the dangerous ability to convince others that handing over their credits is a good idea, even when every instinct screams that they should not.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Of all the rogues one is likely to meet, the Charlatan is the most innocuous. A Charlatan never holds a person at blaster-point, demanding their victims empty out their pockets. A Charlatan that fails to dupe a victim simply moves on to find easier prey. In fact, in some corners of the galaxy, Charlatans are regarded as heroic, especially those who rip off folks who are just as corrupt as they are.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Individuals become Charlatans not out of greed or want, but because their talents are well suited for espionage. Spies, infiltrators, and other intelligence agents can also double as Charlatans to mask their true intentions while trying to learn information, acquire a precious object, or sabotage an enemy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Examples of Charlatans in Star Wars:"]}," Achk Med-Beq, Dannl Faytonni, Lando Calrissian, Orloc.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," To qualify to become a Charlatan, a character must fulfill the following criteria:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Minimum Level:"]}," 7th"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Trained Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained_Skills"},":"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Deception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Deception","referenceId":"reference:17455029fb9994a3"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"},":"]}," Any one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent"}," from the\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Disgrace Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disgrace_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:934cf1fece146b2a"},","]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Influence Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Influence_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:c995726a33a2e905"},", or"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Lineage Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lineage_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:9d6af76576dc4c6e"}]}]}]}]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Game Rule Information"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Charlatans have the following game statistics: \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","c